1. DEFINITIONS

"Software" means Retake: its source code, compiled libraries (AAR, JAR), documentation,
and the bundled model, which includes the model weights, tokenizer, vocabularies, label and
text lists, and the file formats that store them (together, the "Model").

"Licensor" or "Hoverfly" means the copyright holder of the Software.

"You" means the person or legal entity that uses the Software.

"Product" means an application, website, service or device that You build, publish or
operate and that includes or uses the Software. Versions and editions of the same
application offered under the same name count as one Product.

"Platform" means an operating environment on which a Product runs, such as Android, iOS,
the web, desktop or an embedded device.

"Monthly Active Devices" means the number of distinct devices on which a Product runs the
Software at least once during a calendar month, counted separately for each Product and
each Platform. How often the Software runs on a device does not matter.


2. FREE COMMUNITY LICENSE

Subject to the terms of this license, Hoverfly grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive,
non-transferable, non-sublicensable, royalty-free license to:

  (a) use, copy and run the Software; and
  (b) distribute the Software in compiled form as part of Your Product, including in a
      commercial Product,

provided that no Product of Yours exceeds 10,000 Monthly Active Devices on any Platform.

No API key, registration, license file or payment is required for this free license.

You may change the Software's source code (but not the Model) to integrate it into, or fix
problems in, Your own Product. You may not distribute modified source code on its own.


3. COMMERCIAL LICENSE

If a Product exceeds 10,000 Monthly Active Devices on any Platform, You must obtain a
separate written commercial license from Hoverfly for that Product before continuing to
use or distribute the Software in it. You have 30 days from the end of the first month in
which the limit was exceeded to obtain it.

A commercial license covers one Product and one Hoverfly library, unless the written
agreement says otherwise. Contact Hoverfly at the address at the top of this license.


4. RESTRICTIONS

Under the free license and any commercial license (unless a written agreement with
Hoverfly expressly allows it), You may not:

  (a) Resale. Sell, rent, lease, sublicense or otherwise redistribute the Software or the
      Model on its own, or as part of a library, SDK, framework, model collection or
      developer tool whose purpose is to give others access to the Software's features.

  (b) Weights. Extract, copy, export, publish or share the Model separately from Your
      Product, or modify, fine-tune, retrain, prune, quantize, merge, convert or otherwise
      change the Model or create a derivative of it.

  (c) Distillation and training. Use the Software, the Model, or any output produced by
      them to train, fine-tune, distill, evaluate for the purpose of replicating, or
      otherwise improve any machine learning model, other than the Model as supplied by
      Hoverfly.

  (d) Reverse engineering. Decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the Model, its
      weights or its file formats, or attempt to recover how the Model was built, except
      to the extent that applicable law expressly permits this despite this restriction.

  (e) Hosted access. Offer the Software or the Model as a hosted service, API or cloud
      endpoint that lets third parties send inputs and receive its outputs.

  (f) Competing products. Use the Software or the Model to build a product that competes
      with the Software.

  (g) Notices. Remove, hide or change any copyright notice, license text or attribution in
      the Software.

  (h) Workarounds. Split a Product into several Products, or use similar arrangements, to
      stay under the Monthly Active Devices limit.

  (i) Unlawful use. Use the Software in violation of any applicable law.


